window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b343-c2f8498103bdcb1a.json"]={sha256:"c2f8498103bdcb1aeaa39445e2628849e8c8a5290447a0805d9968a3b9cd02c1",value:{"id":"b343","title":"軌道道碴搗固整正","titleEn":"Ballast tamping and track alignment","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"軌道道碴搗固整正以「道碴重排支承恢復與幾何保真」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。搗固把道碴重新配置到軌枕下方以恢復支承，起道後的幾何和重載後的幾何並非同一件事；必須把短期整正與長期沉陷追蹤連在一起。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops ballast rearrangement support recovery and geometry fidelity through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Tamping rearranges ballast beneath sleepers to restore support, but geometry immediately after lifting differs from geometry after traffic; short-term correction must therefore be connected with settlement monitoring. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["軌道幾何","Track geometry"],["搗固作用","Tamping action"],["道碴接觸","Ballast contact"],["支承剛度","Support stiffness"],["整正復測","Correction survey"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["軌道幾何","搗固作用","道碴接觸","支承剛度","整正復測"],"labelsEn":["Track geometry","Tamping action","Ballast contact","Support stiffness","Correction survey"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s；y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h。只把 sleepers 增加一個整數單位，y=1350 sleepers/h。模型邊界：每循環處理數固定且無停機；僅為理想連續產能；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m；y=A*gap*1000=2 litre。只把 A 增加百分之十，y=2.2 litre。模型邊界：空隙以面積上的平均值代表；不描述局部懸空或顆粒排列；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s; y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h. Increasing only sleepers with an increase of one whole unit gives y=1350 sleepers/h. Boundary: Fixed units per cycle and no downtime; ideal continuous throughput only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m; y=A*gap*1000=2 litre. Increasing only A with a ten-percent increase gives y=2.2 litre. Boundary: Gap is represented by its area-average value; local voids and particle arrangement are not resolved; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b343-v16-s1","title":"搗固循環產能與軌枕底空隙量","titleEn":"Tamping cycle productivity & Under-sleeper void volume","description":"本階段聚焦「搗固循環產能」與「軌枕底空隙量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tamping cycle productivity\" and \"Under-sleeper void volume\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b343-v16-01","title":"搗固循環產能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tamping cycle productivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「搗固循環產能」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tamping cycle productivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單循環處理數乘循環頻率只是理想產能。本模型把 sleepers 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加一個整數單位，輸出增加為 1350 sleepers/h。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。每循環處理數固定且無停機；僅為理想連續產能。使用實際循環與停機時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「搗固循環產能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Units per cycle times cycle frequency gives ideal productivity only. In this model, sleepers is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. An increase of one whole unit means the output increases to 1350 sleepers/h. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Fixed units per cycle and no downtime; ideal continuous throughput only. Use actual cycles and downtime as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tamping cycle productivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s；y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s; y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「搗固循環產能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tamping cycle productivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-01-k1","title":"搗固循環產能","titleEn":"Tamping cycle productivity","text":"單循環處理數乘循環頻率只是理想產能。本模型把 sleepers 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加一個整數單位，輸出增加為 1350 sleepers/h。","textEn":"Units per cycle times cycle frequency gives ideal productivity only. In this model, sleepers is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「搗固循環產能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tamping cycle productivity\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能","單循環處理數乘循環頻率只是理想產能。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity.","Units per cycle times cycle frequency gives ideal productivity only.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單循環處理數乘循環頻率只是理想產能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Units per cycle times cycle frequency gives ideal productivity only. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b343-v16-02","title":"搗固循環產能：定量估算","titleEn":"Tamping cycle productivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「搗固循環產能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tamping cycle productivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s；y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h。只把 sleepers 增加一個整數單位，y=1350 sleepers/h。模型邊界：每循環處理數固定且無停機；僅為理想連續產能；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s; y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h. Increasing only sleepers with an increase of one whole unit gives y=1350 sleepers/h. Boundary: Fixed units per cycle and no downtime; ideal continuous throughput only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以實際循環與停機時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成循環起訖時間、每次軌枕數及停機原因帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use actual cycles and downtime to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s；y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h。只把 sleepers 增加一個整數單位，y=1350 sleepers/h。模型邊界：每循環處理數固定且無停機；僅為理想連續產能；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s; y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h. Increasing only sleepers with an increase of one whole unit gives y=1350 sleepers/h. Boundary: Fixed units per cycle and no downtime; ideal continuous throughput only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「搗固循環產能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tamping cycle productivity\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s; y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s；y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: sleepers=2 count, cycle=8 s; y=sleepers*3600/cycle=900 sleepers/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b343-v16-03","title":"搗固循環產能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tamping cycle productivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「搗固循環產能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tamping cycle productivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以實際循環與停機時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成循環起訖時間、每次軌枕數及停機原因帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「搗固循環產能」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use actual cycles and downtime to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic cycle start-end times, sleeper counts and downtime records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Tamping cycle productivity. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「搗固循環產能」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出每循環處理數固定且無停機；僅為理想連續產能如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能造成偏離的合成觀察，以實際循環與停機時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Tamping cycle productivity, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed units per cycle and no downtime; ideal continuous throughput only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity. Explain which evidence in actual cycles and downtime distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以實際循環與停機時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成循環起訖時間、每次軌枕數及停機原因帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「搗固循環產能」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use actual cycles and downtime to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic cycle start-end times, sleeper counts and downtime records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Tamping cycle productivity. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「搗固循環產能」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出每循環處理數固定且無停機；僅為理想連續產能如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能造成偏離的合成觀察，以實際循環與停機時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Tamping cycle productivity, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed units per cycle and no downtime; ideal continuous throughput only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity. Explain which evidence in actual cycles and downtime distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「搗固循環產能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tamping cycle productivity\"?","options":["本單元以實際循環與停機時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成循環起訖時間、每次軌枕數及停機原因帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化"],"optionsEn":["Use actual cycles and downtime to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以實際循環與停機時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成循環起訖時間、每次軌枕數及停機原因帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use actual cycles and downtime to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b343-v16-04","title":"搗固循環產能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tamping cycle productivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「搗固循環產能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tamping cycle productivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能。這個失效與「搗固循環產能」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查實際循環與停機時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity. This failure and a measurement bias in Tamping cycle productivity can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check actual cycles and downtime rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用實際循環與停機時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能。這個失效與「搗固循環產能」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查實際循環與停機時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity. This failure and a measurement bias in Tamping cycle productivity can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check actual cycles and downtime rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「搗固循環產能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tamping cycle productivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b343-v16-05","title":"軌枕底空隙量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Under-sleeper void volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「軌枕底空隙量」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Under-sleeper void volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"面積乘平均空隙描述需重新支承的體積量級。本模型把 A 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 2.2 litre。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。空隙以面積上的平均值代表；不描述局部懸空或顆粒排列。使用支承接觸與空隙剖面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「軌枕底空隙量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Area times average gap describes the volume scale requiring renewed support. In this model, A is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 2.2 litre. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Gap is represented by its area-average value; local voids and particle arrangement are not resolved. Use support contact and gap profile as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. An average gap hides local unsupported regions; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Under-sleeper void volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m；y=A*gap*1000=2 litre。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m; y=A*gap*1000=2 litre.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「軌枕底空隙量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Under-sleeper void volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-05-k1","title":"軌枕底空隙量","titleEn":"Under-sleeper void volume","text":"面積乘平均空隙描述需重新支承的體積量級。本模型把 A 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 2.2 litre。","textEn":"Area times average gap describes the volume scale requiring renewed support. In this model, A is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軌枕底空隙量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Under-sleeper void volume\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承","面積乘平均空隙描述需重新支承的體積量級。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.","Area times average gap describes the volume scale requiring renewed support."],"answer":2,"explanation":"面積乘平均空隙描述需重新支承的體積量級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Area times average gap describes the volume scale requiring renewed support. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b343-v16-06","title":"軌枕底空隙量：定量估算","titleEn":"Under-sleeper void volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軌枕底空隙量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Under-sleeper void volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m；y=A*gap*1000=2 litre。只把 A 增加百分之十，y=2.2 litre。模型邊界：空隙以面積上的平均值代表；不描述局部懸空或顆粒排列；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m; y=A*gap*1000=2 litre. Increasing only A with a ten-percent increase gives y=2.2 litre. Boundary: Gap is represented by its area-average value; local voids and particle arrangement are not resolved; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以支承接觸與空隙剖面區分模型與觀察，先用透明顆粒模型、接觸壓痕及多點空隙厚度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use support contact and gap profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m；y=A*gap*1000=2 litre。只把 A 增加百分之十，y=2.2 litre。模型邊界：空隙以面積上的平均值代表；不描述局部懸空或顆粒排列；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m; y=A*gap*1000=2 litre. Increasing only A with a ten-percent increase gives y=2.2 litre. Boundary: Gap is represented by its area-average value; local voids and particle arrangement are not resolved; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軌枕底空隙量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Under-sleeper void volume\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m；y=A*gap*1000=2 litre。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m; y=A*gap*1000=2 litre.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m；y=A*gap*1000=2 litre。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=0.5 m2, gap=0.004 m; y=A*gap*1000=2 litre. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b343-v16-07","title":"軌枕底空隙量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Under-sleeper void volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「軌枕底空隙量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Under-sleeper void volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以支承接觸與空隙剖面區分模型與觀察，先用透明顆粒模型、接觸壓痕及多點空隙厚度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌枕底空隙量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use support contact and gap profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using transparent granular model, contact imprints and gap thickness at multiple points, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Under-sleeper void volume. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「軌枕底空隙量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出空隙以面積上的平均值代表；不描述局部懸空或顆粒排列如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空造成偏離的合成觀察，以支承接觸與空隙剖面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Under-sleeper void volume, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Gap is represented by its area-average value; local voids and particle arrangement are not resolved. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions. Explain which evidence in support contact and gap profile distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An average gap hides local unsupported regions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以支承接觸與空隙剖面區分模型與觀察，先用透明顆粒模型、接觸壓痕及多點空隙厚度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌枕底空隙量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use support contact and gap profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using transparent granular model, contact imprints and gap thickness at multiple points, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Under-sleeper void volume. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「軌枕底空隙量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出空隙以面積上的平均值代表；不描述局部懸空或顆粒排列如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空造成偏離的合成觀察，以支承接觸與空隙剖面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Under-sleeper void volume, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Gap is represented by its area-average value; local voids and particle arrangement are not resolved. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions. Explain which evidence in support contact and gap profile distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軌枕底空隙量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Under-sleeper void volume\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以支承接觸與空隙剖面區分模型與觀察，先用透明顆粒模型、接觸壓痕及多點空隙厚度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use support contact and gap profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以支承接觸與空隙剖面區分模型與觀察，先用透明顆粒模型、接觸壓痕及多點空隙厚度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use support contact and gap profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b343-v16-08","title":"軌枕底空隙量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Under-sleeper void volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軌枕底空隙量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Under-sleeper void volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空。這個失效與「軌枕底空隙量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支承接觸與空隙剖面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An average gap hides local unsupported regions. This failure and a measurement bias in Under-sleeper void volume can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support contact and gap profile rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用支承接觸與空隙剖面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An average gap hides local unsupported regions; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空。這個失效與「軌枕底空隙量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支承接觸與空隙剖面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"An average gap hides local unsupported regions. This failure and a measurement bias in Under-sleeper void volume can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support contact and gap profile rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軌枕底空隙量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Under-sleeper void volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承","平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.","An average gap hides local unsupported regions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An average gap hides local unsupported regions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b343-v16-s2","title":"擠壓平均接觸壓與模型擠壓作功","titleEn":"Mean squeeze contact pressure & Model squeeze work","description":"本階段聚焦「擠壓平均接觸壓」與「模型擠壓作功」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mean squeeze contact pressure\" and \"Model squeeze work\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b343-v16-09","title":"擠壓平均接觸壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mean squeeze contact pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「擠壓平均接觸壓」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mean squeeze contact pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平均壓力不能代表個別顆粒接觸點壓力。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 440 kPa。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。名義接觸面積已知且合力準靜態；不代表顆粒點接觸應力。使用力與接觸範圍作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「擠壓平均接觸壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean pressure does not represent individual grain-contact pressure. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 440 kPa. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Nominal area is known and resultant force quasistatic; particle point-contact stresses are not represented. Use force and contact extent as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mean squeeze contact pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2；y=F/A=400 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2; y=F/A=400 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「擠壓平均接觸壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mean squeeze contact pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-09-k1","title":"擠壓平均接觸壓","titleEn":"Mean squeeze contact pressure","text":"平均壓力不能代表個別顆粒接觸點壓力。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 440 kPa。","textEn":"Mean pressure does not represent individual grain-contact pressure. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「擠壓平均接觸壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mean squeeze contact pressure\" is correct?","options":["平均壓力不能代表個別顆粒接觸點壓力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質"],"optionsEn":["Mean pressure does not represent individual grain-contact pressure.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均壓力不能代表個別顆粒接觸點壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean pressure does not represent individual grain-contact pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b343-v16-10","title":"擠壓平均接觸壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Mean squeeze contact pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擠壓平均接觸壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mean squeeze contact pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2；y=F/A=400 kPa。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=440 kPa。模型邊界：名義接觸面積已知且合力準靜態；不代表顆粒點接觸應力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2; y=F/A=400 kPa. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=440 kPa. Boundary: Nominal area is known and resultant force quasistatic; particle point-contact stresses are not represented; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以力與接觸範圍區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、接觸印跡面積及碎粒前後篩分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use force and contact extent to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2；y=F/A=400 kPa。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=440 kPa。模型邊界：名義接觸面積已知且合力準靜態；不代表顆粒點接觸應力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2; y=F/A=400 kPa. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=440 kPa. Boundary: Nominal area is known and resultant force quasistatic; particle point-contact stresses are not represented; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「擠壓平均接觸壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mean squeeze contact pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2；y=F/A=400 kPa。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2; y=F/A=400 kPa.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2；y=F/A=400 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=8 kN, A=0.02 m2; y=F/A=400 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b343-v16-11","title":"擠壓平均接觸壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mean squeeze contact pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擠壓平均接觸壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mean squeeze contact pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以力與接觸範圍區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、接觸印跡面積及碎粒前後篩分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「擠壓平均接觸壓」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use force and contact extent to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load model force gauge, contact-imprint area and before-after particle grading, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mean squeeze contact pressure. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「擠壓平均接觸壓」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出名義接觸面積已知且合力準靜態；不代表顆粒點接觸應力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承造成偏離的合成觀察，以力與接觸範圍說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mean squeeze contact pressure, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Nominal area is known and resultant force quasistatic; particle point-contact stresses are not represented. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support. Explain which evidence in force and contact extent distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以力與接觸範圍區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、接觸印跡面積及碎粒前後篩分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「擠壓平均接觸壓」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use force and contact extent to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load model force gauge, contact-imprint area and before-after particle grading, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mean squeeze contact pressure. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「擠壓平均接觸壓」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出名義接觸面積已知且合力準靜態；不代表顆粒點接觸應力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承造成偏離的合成觀察，以力與接觸範圍說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mean squeeze contact pressure, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Nominal area is known and resultant force quasistatic; particle point-contact stresses are not represented. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support. Explain which evidence in force and contact extent distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「擠壓平均接觸壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mean squeeze contact pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷","本單元以力與接觸範圍區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、接觸印跡面積及碎粒前後篩分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects.","Use force and contact extent to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以力與接觸範圍區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、接觸印跡面積及碎粒前後篩分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use force and contact extent to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b343-v16-12","title":"擠壓平均接觸壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mean squeeze contact pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擠壓平均接觸壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mean squeeze contact pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承。這個失效與「擠壓平均接觸壓」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查力與接觸範圍，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support. This failure and a measurement bias in Mean squeeze contact pressure can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check force and contact extent rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用力與接觸範圍作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承。這個失效與「擠壓平均接觸壓」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查力與接觸範圍，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support. This failure and a measurement bias in Mean squeeze contact pressure can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check force and contact extent rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「擠壓平均接觸壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mean squeeze contact pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質"],"optionsEn":["Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b343-v16-13","title":"模型擠壓作功：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Model squeeze work: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「模型擠壓作功」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Model squeeze work” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"力位移積分描述機械輸入，並非全部能量都用於有效重排。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 17.6 J。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。力是行程內的代表平均值；只算外部機械作功。使用力位移迴圈作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「模型擠壓作功」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Force-displacement integration describes mechanical input, but not all energy produces useful rearrangement. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 17.6 J. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Force is the representative average over travel; only external mechanical work is included. Use force-displacement loops as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Model squeeze work” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 N, x=0.02 m；y=F*x=16 J。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 N, x=0.02 m; y=F*x=16 J.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「模型擠壓作功」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Model squeeze work”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-13-k1","title":"模型擠壓作功","titleEn":"Model squeeze work","text":"力位移積分描述機械輸入，並非全部能量都用於有效重排。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 17.6 J。","textEn":"Force-displacement integration describes mechanical input, but not all energy produces useful rearrangement. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型擠壓作功」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Model squeeze work\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質","力位移積分描述機械輸入，並非全部能量都用於有效重排。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality.","Force-displacement integration describes mechanical input, but not all energy produces useful rearrangement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"力位移積分描述機械輸入，並非全部能量都用於有效重排。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Force-displacement integration describes mechanical input, but not all energy produces useful rearrangement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b343-v16-14","title":"模型擠壓作功：定量估算","titleEn":"Model squeeze work: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模型擠壓作功」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Model squeeze work” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 N, x=0.02 m；y=F*x=16 J。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=17.6 J。模型邊界：力是行程內的代表平均值；只算外部機械作功；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 N, x=0.02 m; y=F*x=16 J. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=17.6 J. Boundary: Force is the representative average over travel; only external mechanical work is included; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以力位移迴圈區分模型與觀察，先用模型同步力位移取樣與迴圈積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use force-displacement loops to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 N, x=0.02 m；y=F*x=16 J。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=17.6 J。模型邊界：力是行程內的代表平均值；只算外部機械作功；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 N, x=0.02 m; y=F*x=16 J. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=17.6 J. Boundary: Force is the representative average over travel; only external mechanical work is included; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模型擠壓作功」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Model squeeze work\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 N, x=0.02 m；y=F*x=16 J。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 N, x=0.02 m; y=F*x=16 J."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 N, x=0.02 m；y=F*x=16 J。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 N, x=0.02 m; y=F*x=16 J. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b343-v16-15","title":"模型擠壓作功：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Model squeeze work: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模型擠壓作功」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Model squeeze work” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以力位移迴圈區分模型與觀察，先用模型同步力位移取樣與迴圈積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「模型擠壓作功」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use force-displacement loops to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synchronized model force-displacement samples and loop integration, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Model squeeze work. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「模型擠壓作功」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出力是行程內的代表平均值；只算外部機械作功如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質造成偏離的合成觀察，以力位移迴圈說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Model squeeze work, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Force is the representative average over travel; only external mechanical work is included. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality. Explain which evidence in force-displacement loops distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以力位移迴圈區分模型與觀察，先用模型同步力位移取樣與迴圈積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「模型擠壓作功」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use force-displacement loops to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synchronized model force-displacement samples and loop integration, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Model squeeze work. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「模型擠壓作功」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出力是行程內的代表平均值；只算外部機械作功如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質造成偏離的合成觀察，以力位移迴圈說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Model squeeze work, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Force is the representative average over travel; only external mechanical work is included. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality. Explain which evidence in force-displacement loops distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模型擠壓作功」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Model squeeze work\"?","options":["本單元以力位移迴圈區分模型與觀察，先用模型同步力位移取樣與迴圈積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能"],"optionsEn":["Use force-displacement loops to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以力位移迴圈區分模型與觀察，先用模型同步力位移取樣與迴圈積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use force-displacement loops to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b343-v16-16","title":"模型擠壓作功：失效診斷","titleEn":"Model squeeze work: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模型擠壓作功」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Model squeeze work” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質。這個失效與「模型擠壓作功」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查力位移迴圈，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality. This failure and a measurement bias in Model squeeze work can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check force-displacement loops rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用力位移迴圈作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質。這個失效與「模型擠壓作功」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查力位移迴圈，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality. This failure and a measurement bias in Model squeeze work can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check force-displacement loops rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型擠壓作功」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Model squeeze work\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b343-v16-s3","title":"振動週期次數與起道量分配","titleEn":"Vibration cycle count & Lift allocation","description":"本階段聚焦「振動週期次數」與「起道量分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Vibration cycle count\" and \"Lift allocation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b343-v16-17","title":"振動週期次數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Vibration cycle count: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「振動週期次數」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vibration cycle count” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"頻率乘持續時間給出循環次數，不等同填充程度。本模型把 f 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 46.2 cycles。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。頻率固定且無中斷；循環數不代表填充品質。使用振動與填充位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「振動週期次數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Frequency times duration gives cycle count, not degree of filling. In this model, f is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 46.2 cycles. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Frequency is constant without interruption; cycle count does not establish filling quality. Use vibration and filling movement as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Vibration cycle count” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s；y=f*t=42 cycles。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s; y=f*t=42 cycles.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「振動週期次數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Vibration cycle count”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-17-k1","title":"振動週期次數","titleEn":"Vibration cycle count","text":"頻率乘持續時間給出循環次數，不等同填充程度。本模型把 f 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 46.2 cycles。","textEn":"Frequency times duration gives cycle count, not degree of filling. In this model, f is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「振動週期次數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vibration cycle count\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真","頻率乘持續時間給出循環次數，不等同填充程度。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.","Frequency times duration gives cycle count, not degree of filling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"頻率乘持續時間給出循環次數，不等同填充程度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Frequency times duration gives cycle count, not degree of filling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b343-v16-18","title":"振動週期次數：定量估算","titleEn":"Vibration cycle count: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「振動週期次數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vibration cycle count” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s；y=f*t=42 cycles。只把 f 增加百分之十，y=46.2 cycles。模型邊界：頻率固定且無中斷；循環數不代表填充品質；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s; y=f*t=42 cycles. Increasing only f with a ten-percent increase gives y=46.2 cycles. Boundary: Frequency is constant without interruption; cycle count does not establish filling quality; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以振動與填充位移區分模型與觀察，先用合成振動時間序列、過零計數與獨立填充位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use vibration and filling movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s；y=f*t=42 cycles。只把 f 增加百分之十，y=46.2 cycles。模型邊界：頻率固定且無中斷；循環數不代表填充品質；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s; y=f*t=42 cycles. Increasing only f with a ten-percent increase gives y=46.2 cycles. Boundary: Frequency is constant without interruption; cycle count does not establish filling quality; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「振動週期次數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vibration cycle count\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s；y=f*t=42 cycles。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s; y=f*t=42 cycles.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s；y=f*t=42 cycles。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=35 Hz, t=1.2 s; y=f*t=42 cycles. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b343-v16-19","title":"振動週期次數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vibration cycle count: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「振動週期次數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vibration cycle count” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以振動與填充位移區分模型與觀察，先用合成振動時間序列、過零計數與獨立填充位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「振動週期次數」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use vibration and filling movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic vibration history, zero-crossing count and independent filling displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Vibration cycle count. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「振動週期次數」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出頻率固定且無中斷；循環數不代表填充品質如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承造成偏離的合成觀察，以振動與填充位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Vibration cycle count, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Frequency is constant without interruption; cycle count does not establish filling quality. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support. Explain which evidence in vibration and filling movement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以振動與填充位移區分模型與觀察，先用合成振動時間序列、過零計數與獨立填充位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「振動週期次數」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use vibration and filling movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic vibration history, zero-crossing count and independent filling displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Vibration cycle count. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「振動週期次數」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出頻率固定且無中斷；循環數不代表填充品質如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承造成偏離的合成觀察，以振動與填充位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Vibration cycle count, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Frequency is constant without interruption; cycle count does not establish filling quality. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support. Explain which evidence in vibration and filling movement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「振動週期次數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vibration cycle count\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以振動與填充位移區分模型與觀察，先用合成振動時間序列、過零計數與獨立填充位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use vibration and filling movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以振動與填充位移區分模型與觀察，先用合成振動時間序列、過零計數與獨立填充位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use vibration and filling movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b343-v16-20","title":"振動週期次數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vibration cycle count: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「振動週期次數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vibration cycle count” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承。這個失效與「振動週期次數」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查振動與填充位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support. This failure and a measurement bias in Vibration cycle count can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check vibration and filling movement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用振動與填充位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承。這個失效與「振動週期次數」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查振動與填充位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support. This failure and a measurement bias in Vibration cycle count can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check vibration and filling movement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「振動週期次數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vibration cycle count\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真","重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.","Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b343-v16-21","title":"起道量分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lift allocation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「起道量分配」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lift allocation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"目標與現況差值需同一高程基準。本模型把 target 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 9.2 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。目標與現況高程使用同一固定基準；不含後續回沉。使用整正前後同基準高程作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；基準移動會使起道量失真，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「起道量分配」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Target-minus-existing lift requires a common elevation datum. In this model, target is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 9.2 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Target and existing elevations share a fixed datum; later settlement is excluded. Use before-and-after levels on the same datum as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lift allocation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=12 mm, existing=4 mm；y=target-existing=8 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=12 mm, existing=4 mm; y=target-existing=8 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「起道量分配」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lift allocation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-21-k1","title":"起道量分配","titleEn":"Lift allocation","text":"目標與現況差值需同一高程基準。本模型把 target 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 9.2 mm。","textEn":"Target-minus-existing lift requires a common elevation datum. In this model, target is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「起道量分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lift allocation\" is correct?","options":["目標與現況差值需同一高程基準。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較"],"optionsEn":["Target-minus-existing lift requires a common elevation datum.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"目標與現況差值需同一高程基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Target-minus-existing lift requires a common elevation datum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b343-v16-22","title":"起道量分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Lift allocation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「起道量分配」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lift allocation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=12 mm, existing=4 mm；y=target-existing=8 mm。只把 target 增加百分之十，y=9.2 mm。模型邊界：目標與現況高程使用同一固定基準；不含後續回沉；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=12 mm, existing=4 mm; y=target-existing=8 mm. Increasing only target with a ten-percent increase gives y=9.2 mm. Boundary: Target and existing elevations share a fixed datum; later settlement is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以整正前後同基準高程區分模型與觀察，先用模型固定水準點、整正前後高程及基準穩定性建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use before-and-after levels on the same datum to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=12 mm, existing=4 mm；y=target-existing=8 mm。只把 target 增加百分之十，y=9.2 mm。模型邊界：目標與現況高程使用同一固定基準；不含後續回沉；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=12 mm, existing=4 mm; y=target-existing=8 mm. Increasing only target with a ten-percent increase gives y=9.2 mm. Boundary: Target and existing elevations share a fixed datum; later settlement is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「起道量分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lift allocation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=12 mm, existing=4 mm；y=target-existing=8 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=12 mm, existing=4 mm; y=target-existing=8 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=12 mm, existing=4 mm；y=target-existing=8 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=12 mm, existing=4 mm; y=target-existing=8 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b343-v16-23","title":"起道量分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lift allocation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「起道量分配」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lift allocation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以整正前後同基準高程區分模型與觀察，先用模型固定水準點、整正前後高程及基準穩定性建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「起道量分配」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use before-and-after levels on the same datum to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using fixed model benchmarks, before-after elevations and datum stability, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Lift allocation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「起道量分配」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出目標與現況高程使用同一固定基準；不含後續回沉如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由基準移動會使起道量失真造成偏離的合成觀察，以整正前後同基準高程說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Lift allocation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Target and existing elevations share a fixed datum; later settlement is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift. Explain which evidence in before-and-after levels on the same datum distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：基準移動會使起道量失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以整正前後同基準高程區分模型與觀察，先用模型固定水準點、整正前後高程及基準穩定性建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「起道量分配」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use before-and-after levels on the same datum to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using fixed model benchmarks, before-after elevations and datum stability, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Lift allocation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「起道量分配」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出目標與現況高程使用同一固定基準；不含後續回沉如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由基準移動會使起道量失真造成偏離的合成觀察，以整正前後同基準高程說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Lift allocation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Target and existing elevations share a fixed datum; later settlement is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift. Explain which evidence in before-and-after levels on the same datum distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「起道量分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lift allocation\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承","本單元以整正前後同基準高程區分模型與觀察，先用模型固定水準點、整正前後高程及基準穩定性建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.","Use before-and-after levels on the same datum to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以整正前後同基準高程區分模型與觀察，先用模型固定水準點、整正前後高程及基準穩定性建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use before-and-after levels on the same datum to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b343-v16-24","title":"起道量分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lift allocation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「起道量分配」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lift allocation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基準移動會使起道量失真。這個失效與「起道量分配」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查整正前後同基準高程，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift. This failure and a measurement bias in Lift allocation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check before-and-after levels on the same datum rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用整正前後同基準高程作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；基準移動會使起道量失真，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基準移動會使起道量失真。這個失效與「起道量分配」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查整正前後同基準高程，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift. This failure and a measurement bias in Lift allocation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check before-and-after levels on the same datum rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「起道量分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lift allocation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["基準移動會使起道量失真。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較"],"optionsEn":["A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"基準移動會使起道量失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b343-v16-s4","title":"整正後回沉率與道碴橫向排水","titleEn":"Post-correction settlement ratio & Ballast lateral drainage scale","description":"本階段聚焦「整正後回沉率」與「道碴橫向排水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Post-correction settlement ratio\" and \"Ballast lateral drainage scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b343-v16-25","title":"整正後回沉率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Post-correction settlement ratio: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「整正後回沉率」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-correction settlement ratio” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"回沉比例描述短期保留量，不預測無限期穩定。本模型把 settled 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.5 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。回沉與起道量使用同一基準和指定觀測期間。使用通車荷載量與高程趨勢作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「整正後回沉率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Settlement fraction describes short-term retention and does not predict indefinite stability. In this model, settled is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 27.5 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Settlement and lift share a datum and a specified observation period. Use traffic loading and elevation trend as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Post-correction settlement ratio” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm；y=settled/lift*100=25 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm; y=settled/lift*100=25 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「整正後回沉率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Post-correction settlement ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-25-k1","title":"整正後回沉率","titleEn":"Post-correction settlement ratio","text":"回沉比例描述短期保留量，不預測無限期穩定。本模型把 settled 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.5 percent。","textEn":"Settlement fraction describes short-term retention and does not predict indefinite stability. In this model, settled is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「整正後回沉率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Post-correction settlement ratio\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較","回沉比例描述短期保留量，不預測無限期穩定。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable.","Settlement fraction describes short-term retention and does not predict indefinite stability.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回沉比例描述短期保留量，不預測無限期穩定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Settlement fraction describes short-term retention and does not predict indefinite stability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b343-v16-26","title":"整正後回沉率：定量估算","titleEn":"Post-correction settlement ratio: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「整正後回沉率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-correction settlement ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm；y=settled/lift*100=25 percent。只把 settled 增加百分之十，y=27.5 percent。模型邊界：回沉與起道量使用同一基準和指定觀測期間；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm; y=settled/lift*100=25 percent. Increasing only settled with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.5 percent. Boundary: Settlement and lift share a datum and a specified observation period; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以通車荷載量與高程趨勢區分模型與觀察，先用逐期高程、模型循環載荷與累積通過噸位帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use traffic loading and elevation trend to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm；y=settled/lift*100=25 percent。只把 settled 增加百分之十，y=27.5 percent。模型邊界：回沉與起道量使用同一基準和指定觀測期間；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm; y=settled/lift*100=25 percent. Increasing only settled with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.5 percent. Boundary: Settlement and lift share a datum and a specified observation period; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「整正後回沉率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Post-correction settlement ratio\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm；y=settled/lift*100=25 percent。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm; y=settled/lift*100=25 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm；y=settled/lift*100=25 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: settled=3 mm, lift=12 mm; y=settled/lift*100=25 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b343-v16-27","title":"整正後回沉率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Post-correction settlement ratio: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「整正後回沉率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-correction settlement ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以通車荷載量與高程趨勢區分模型與觀察，先用逐期高程、模型循環載荷與累積通過噸位帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「整正後回沉率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use traffic loading and elevation trend to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using periodic elevations, model loading cycles and cumulative traffic-tonnage account, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Post-correction settlement ratio. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「整正後回沉率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出回沉與起道量使用同一基準和指定觀測期間如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較造成偏離的合成觀察，以通車荷載量與高程趨勢說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Post-correction settlement ratio, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Settlement and lift share a datum and a specified observation period. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable. Explain which evidence in traffic loading and elevation trend distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以通車荷載量與高程趨勢區分模型與觀察，先用逐期高程、模型循環載荷與累積通過噸位帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「整正後回沉率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use traffic loading and elevation trend to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using periodic elevations, model loading cycles and cumulative traffic-tonnage account, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Post-correction settlement ratio. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「整正後回沉率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出回沉與起道量使用同一基準和指定觀測期間如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較造成偏離的合成觀察，以通車荷載量與高程趨勢說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Post-correction settlement ratio, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Settlement and lift share a datum and a specified observation period. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable. Explain which evidence in traffic loading and elevation trend distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「整正後回沉率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Post-correction settlement ratio\"?","options":["本單元以通車荷載量與高程趨勢區分模型與觀察，先用逐期高程、模型循環載荷與累積通過噸位帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質"],"optionsEn":["Use traffic loading and elevation trend to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以通車荷載量與高程趨勢區分模型與觀察，先用逐期高程、模型循環載荷與累積通過噸位帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use traffic loading and elevation trend to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b343-v16-28","title":"整正後回沉率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Post-correction settlement ratio: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「整正後回沉率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-correction settlement ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較。這個失效與「整正後回沉率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查通車荷載量與高程趨勢，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable. This failure and a measurement bias in Post-correction settlement ratio can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check traffic loading and elevation trend rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用通車荷載量與高程趨勢作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較。這個失效與「整正後回沉率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查通車荷載量與高程趨勢，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable. This failure and a measurement bias in Post-correction settlement ratio can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check traffic loading and elevation trend rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「整正後回沉率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Post-correction settlement ratio\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b343-v16-29","title":"道碴橫向排水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ballast lateral drainage scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「道碴橫向排水」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ballast lateral drainage scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"達西量級只適用假設滲流範圍，堵塞會改變等效滲透率。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.0352 litre/s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。飽和且穩態的達西滲流；滲透率與水力梯度固定。使用水頭差與排出流量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「道碴橫向排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A Darcy estimate applies only to its assumed flow regime; clogging changes effective permeability. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.0352 litre/s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Saturated steady Darcy flow with constant permeability and hydraulic gradient. Use head difference and discharged flow as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ballast lateral drainage scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1；y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1; y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「道碴橫向排水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ballast lateral drainage scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-29-k1","title":"道碴橫向排水","titleEn":"Ballast lateral drainage scale","text":"達西量級只適用假設滲流範圍，堵塞會改變等效滲透率。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.0352 litre/s。","textEn":"A Darcy estimate applies only to its assumed flow regime; clogging changes effective permeability. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「道碴橫向排水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ballast lateral drainage scale\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度","達西量級只適用假設滲流範圍，堵塞會改變等效滲透率。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.","A Darcy estimate applies only to its assumed flow regime; clogging changes effective permeability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"達西量級只適用假設滲流範圍，堵塞會改變等效滲透率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A Darcy estimate applies only to its assumed flow regime; clogging changes effective permeability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b343-v16-30","title":"道碴橫向排水：定量估算","titleEn":"Ballast lateral drainage scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「道碴橫向排水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ballast lateral drainage scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1；y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=0.0352 litre/s。模型邊界：飽和且穩態的達西滲流；滲透率與水力梯度固定；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1; y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.0352 litre/s. Boundary: Saturated steady Darcy flow with constant permeability and hydraulic gradient; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以水頭差與排出流量區分模型與觀察，先用低水頭滲流模型、進出口水頭與定時出水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use head difference and discharged flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1；y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=0.0352 litre/s。模型邊界：飽和且穩態的達西滲流；滲透率與水力梯度固定；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1; y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.0352 litre/s. Boundary: Saturated steady Darcy flow with constant permeability and hydraulic gradient; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「道碴橫向排水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ballast lateral drainage scale\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1；y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1; y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1；y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=0.002 m/s, A=0.8 m2, i=0.02 1; y=k*A*i*1000=0.032 litre/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b343-v16-31","title":"道碴橫向排水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ballast lateral drainage scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「道碴橫向排水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ballast lateral drainage scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以水頭差與排出流量區分模型與觀察，先用低水頭滲流模型、進出口水頭與定時出水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「道碴橫向排水」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use head difference and discharged flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-head permeameter model, inlet-outlet heads and timed discharge volume, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ballast lateral drainage scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「道碴橫向排水」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出飽和且穩態的達西滲流；滲透率與水力梯度固定如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化造成偏離的合成觀察，以水頭差與排出流量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ballast lateral drainage scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Saturated steady Darcy flow with constant permeability and hydraulic gradient. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction. Explain which evidence in head difference and discharged flow distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以水頭差與排出流量區分模型與觀察，先用低水頭滲流模型、進出口水頭與定時出水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「道碴橫向排水」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use head difference and discharged flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-head permeameter model, inlet-outlet heads and timed discharge volume, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ballast lateral drainage scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「道碴橫向排水」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出飽和且穩態的達西滲流；滲透率與水力梯度固定如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化造成偏離的合成觀察，以水頭差與排出流量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ballast lateral drainage scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Saturated steady Darcy flow with constant permeability and hydraulic gradient. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction. Explain which evidence in head difference and discharged flow distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「道碴橫向排水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ballast lateral drainage scale\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以水頭差與排出流量區分模型與觀察，先用低水頭滲流模型、進出口水頭與定時出水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use head difference and discharged flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以水頭差與排出流量區分模型與觀察，先用低水頭滲流模型、進出口水頭與定時出水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use head difference and discharged flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b343-v16-32","title":"道碴橫向排水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ballast lateral drainage scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「道碴橫向排水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ballast lateral drainage scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化。這個失效與「道碴橫向排水」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查水頭差與排出流量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction. This failure and a measurement bias in Ballast lateral drainage scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check head difference and discharged flow rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用水頭差與排出流量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化。這個失效與「道碴橫向排水」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查水頭差與排出流量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction. This failure and a measurement bias in Ballast lateral drainage scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check head difference and discharged flow rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「道碴橫向排水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ballast lateral drainage scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度","細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.","Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細料累積會使整正後仍持續軟化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fines accumulation can sustain softening after geometric correction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b343-v16-s5","title":"支承剛度回復與幾何殘差均方根","titleEn":"Support stiffness recovery & Geometry residual RMS","description":"本階段聚焦「支承剛度回復」與「幾何殘差均方根」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Support stiffness recovery\" and \"Geometry residual RMS\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b343-v16-33","title":"支承剛度回復：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support stiffness recovery: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「支承剛度回復」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support stiffness recovery” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"載重位移斜率描述支承剛度而非單純高度。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.5 kN/mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。力位移由共同零點計算割線剛度；不把它當非線性切線剛度。使用重複模型載重曲線作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支承剛度回復」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Load-displacement slope characterizes support stiffness rather than height alone. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 27.5 kN/mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Force and displacement from one origin give secant stiffness, not nonlinear tangent stiffness. Use repeated model loading curves as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support stiffness recovery” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm；y=F/delta=25 kN/mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm; y=F/delta=25 kN/mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支承剛度回復」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support stiffness recovery”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-33-k1","title":"支承剛度回復","titleEn":"Support stiffness recovery","text":"載重位移斜率描述支承剛度而非單純高度。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.5 kN/mm。","textEn":"Load-displacement slope characterizes support stiffness rather than height alone. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支承剛度回復」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support stiffness recovery\" is correct?","options":["載重位移斜率描述支承剛度而非單純高度。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Load-displacement slope characterizes support stiffness rather than height alone.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"載重位移斜率描述支承剛度而非單純高度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Load-displacement slope characterizes support stiffness rather than height alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b343-v16-34","title":"支承剛度回復：定量估算","titleEn":"Support stiffness recovery: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支承剛度回復」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support stiffness recovery” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm；y=F/delta=25 kN/mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=27.5 kN/mm。模型邊界：力位移由共同零點計算割線剛度；不把它當非線性切線剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm; y=F/delta=25 kN/mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.5 kN/mm. Boundary: Force and displacement from one origin give secant stiffness, not nonlinear tangent stiffness; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以重複模型載重曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型多級載入卸載曲線及殘餘位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use repeated model loading curves to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm；y=F/delta=25 kN/mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=27.5 kN/mm。模型邊界：力位移由共同零點計算割線剛度；不把它當非線性切線剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm; y=F/delta=25 kN/mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.5 kN/mm. Boundary: Force and displacement from one origin give secant stiffness, not nonlinear tangent stiffness; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支承剛度回復」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support stiffness recovery\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均空隙會掩蓋局部懸空","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm；y=F/delta=25 kN/mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無效摩擦耗能會使高作功不代表高品質"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An average gap hides local unsupported regions.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm; y=F/delta=25 kN/mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unproductive friction means high work does not prove quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm；y=F/delta=25 kN/mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40 kN, delta=1.6 mm; y=F/delta=25 kN/mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b343-v16-35","title":"支承剛度回復：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support stiffness recovery: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支承剛度回復」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support stiffness recovery” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以重複模型載重曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型多級載入卸載曲線及殘餘位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「支承剛度回復」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use repeated model loading curves to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model multilevel loading-unloading curves and residual displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Support stiffness recovery. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「支承剛度回復」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出力位移由共同零點計算割線剛度；不把它當非線性切線剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度造成偏離的合成觀察，以重複模型載重曲線說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Support stiffness recovery, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Force and displacement from one origin give secant stiffness, not nonlinear tangent stiffness. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses. Explain which evidence in repeated model loading curves distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以重複模型載重曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型多級載入卸載曲線及殘餘位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「支承剛度回復」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use repeated model loading curves to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model multilevel loading-unloading curves and residual displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Support stiffness recovery. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「支承剛度回復」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出力位移由共同零點計算割線剛度；不把它當非線性切線剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度造成偏離的合成觀察，以重複模型載重曲線說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Support stiffness recovery, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Force and displacement from one origin give secant stiffness, not nonlinear tangent stiffness. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses. Explain which evidence in repeated model loading curves distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支承剛度回復」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support stiffness recovery\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：基準移動會使起道量失真","本單元以重複模型載重曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型多級載入卸載曲線及殘餘位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A moving datum corrupts the inferred lift.","Use repeated model loading curves to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以重複模型載重曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型多級載入卸載曲線及殘餘位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use repeated model loading curves to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b343-v16-36","title":"支承剛度回復：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support stiffness recovery: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支承剛度回復」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support stiffness recovery” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度。這個失效與「支承剛度回復」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查重複模型載重曲線，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses. This failure and a measurement bias in Support stiffness recovery can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check repeated model loading curves rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用重複模型載重曲線作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度。這個失效與「支承剛度回復」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查重複模型載重曲線，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses. This failure and a measurement bias in Support stiffness recovery can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check repeated model loading curves rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支承剛度回復」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support stiffness recovery\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷"],"optionsEn":["The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一高程可能隱藏不同承載剛度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The same elevation can conceal different support stiffnesses. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b343-v16-37","title":"幾何殘差均方根：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Geometry residual RMS: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「幾何殘差均方根」如何影響軌道道碴搗固整正的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Geometry residual RMS” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast tamping and track alignment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均方根保留誤差幅度，但仍須檢查局部峰值。本模型把 e1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.75214 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。三點等權且採同一基準；未量測區域及局部最大值另查。使用逐點殘差與位置作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「幾何殘差均方根」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"RMS retains error magnitude but local peaks still require inspection. In this model, e1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1.75214 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Three equally weighted points share a datum; unmeasured regions and local maxima require separate checks. Use pointwise residuals and positions as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. One average quality score hides localized defects; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Geometry residual RMS” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm；y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm; y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「幾何殘差均方根」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Geometry residual RMS”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-37-k1","title":"幾何殘差均方根","titleEn":"Geometry residual RMS","text":"均方根保留誤差幅度，但仍須檢查局部峰值。本模型把 e1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.75214 mm。","textEn":"RMS retains error magnitude but local peaks still require inspection. In this model, e1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「幾何殘差均方根」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Geometry residual RMS\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷","均方根保留誤差幅度，但仍須檢查局部峰值。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects.","RMS retains error magnitude but local peaks still require inspection.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"均方根保留誤差幅度，但仍須檢查局部峰值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"RMS retains error magnitude but local peaks still require inspection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b343-v16-38","title":"幾何殘差均方根：定量估算","titleEn":"Geometry residual RMS: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「幾何殘差均方根」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Geometry residual RMS” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm；y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm。只把 e1 增加百分之十，y=1.75214 mm。模型邊界：三點等權且採同一基準；未量測區域及局部最大值另查；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm; y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm. Increasing only e1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.75214 mm. Boundary: Three equally weighted points share a datum; unmeasured regions and local maxima require separate checks; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以逐點殘差與位置區分模型與觀察，先用逐點里程、高程殘差及感測器零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use pointwise residuals and positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm；y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm。只把 e1 增加百分之十，y=1.75214 mm。模型邊界：三點等權且採同一基準；未量測區域及局部最大值另查；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm; y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm. Increasing only e1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.75214 mm. Boundary: Three equally weighted points share a datum; unmeasured regions and local maxima require separate checks; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「幾何殘差均方根」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Geometry residual RMS\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：顆粒破碎會改變粒徑與長期支承","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重複振動可能只磨耗顆粒而未改善支承","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Grain crushing changes grading and long-term support.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeated vibration may abrade grains without improving support.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm; y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm；y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: e1=1 mm, e2=-2 mm, e3=2 mm; y=sqrt((e1**2+e2**2+e3**2)/3)=1.73205 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b343-v16-39","title":"幾何殘差均方根：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Geometry residual RMS: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「幾何殘差均方根」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Geometry residual RMS” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以逐點殘差與位置區分模型與觀察，先用逐點里程、高程殘差及感測器零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「幾何殘差均方根」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use pointwise residuals and positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using pointwise chainage, elevation residuals and sensor-zero records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Geometry residual RMS. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「幾何殘差均方根」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出三點等權且採同一基準；未量測區域及局部最大值另查如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷造成偏離的合成觀察，以逐點殘差與位置說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Geometry residual RMS, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Three equally weighted points share a datum; unmeasured regions and local maxima require separate checks. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One average quality score hides localized defects. Explain which evidence in pointwise residuals and positions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One average quality score hides localized defects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以逐點殘差與位置區分模型與觀察，先用逐點里程、高程殘差及感測器零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「幾何殘差均方根」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use pointwise residuals and positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using pointwise chainage, elevation residuals and sensor-zero records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Geometry residual RMS. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「幾何殘差均方根」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出三點等權且採同一基準；未量測區域及局部最大值另查如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷造成偏離的合成觀察，以逐點殘差與位置說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Geometry residual RMS, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Three equally weighted points share a datum; unmeasured regions and local maxima require separate checks. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One average quality score hides localized defects. Explain which evidence in pointwise residuals and positions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「幾何殘差均方根」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Geometry residual RMS\"?","options":["本單元以逐點殘差與位置區分模型與觀察，先用逐點里程、高程殘差及感測器零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄通過噸位會讓不同觀測期不可比較"],"optionsEn":["Use pointwise residuals and positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Missing traffic tonnage makes observation periods incomparable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以逐點殘差與位置區分模型與觀察，先用逐點里程、高程殘差及感測器零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use pointwise residuals and positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b343-v16-40","title":"幾何殘差均方根：失效診斷","titleEn":"Geometry residual RMS: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b343-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「幾何殘差均方根」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Geometry residual RMS” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷。這個失效與「幾何殘差均方根」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查逐點殘差與位置，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One average quality score hides localized defects. This failure and a measurement bias in Geometry residual RMS can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check pointwise residuals and positions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用逐點殘差與位置作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: One average quality score hides localized defects; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One average quality score hides localized defects.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b343-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷。這個失效與「幾何殘差均方根」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查逐點殘差與位置，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"One average quality score hides localized defects. This failure and a measurement bias in Geometry residual RMS can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check pointwise residuals and positions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b343-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「幾何殘差均方根」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Geometry residual RMS\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略定位與等待會高估施工產能"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","One average quality score hides localized defects.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting positioning and waiting overstates productivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一平均品質指標會掩蓋尖峰缺陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One average quality score hides localized defects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-tamp","v16s-track-plasser-history","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b343-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b343-en.svg"}};
